# Server Conventions (NestJS)

## Architecture

- One NestJS module per feature domain: `auth`, `users`, `specs`, `graph`, `agent`, `health`, `database`, etc.
- Each module folder contains: `*.module.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`, `*.dto.ts`, and co-located `*.test.ts` files.
- Use NestJS dependency injection for all service dependencies.

## Module Structure

```
server/src/modules/{feature}/
├── {feature}.module.ts        # NestJS module definition
├── {feature}.controller.ts    # HTTP route handlers
├── {feature}.service.ts       # Business logic
├── {feature}.dto.ts           # Request/response DTOs
├── {feature}.guard.ts         # Auth/permission guards (if needed)
├── {feature}.controller.test.ts  # Controller unit tests
└── {feature}.service.test.ts     # Service unit tests
```

## Controllers

- Handle HTTP concerns only: parse request, call service, return response.
- Use decorators: `@Controller`, `@Get`, `@Post`, `@Put`, `@Delete`, `@Param`, `@Body`, `@Query`.
- Use DTOs with `class-validator` decorators for request validation.
- Return typed responses using shared types from `@kg/shared`.

## Services

- Contain all business logic. Controllers delegate to services.
- Inject dependencies via constructor: `constructor(private readonly fooService: FooService)`.
- Use `@Injectable()` decorator.
- Throw NestJS exceptions (`NotFoundException`, `ForbiddenException`, etc.) for error cases.

## Database

- Use Drizzle ORM with the `DRIZZLE` injection token from `DatabaseModule`.
- Inject via `@Inject(DRIZZLE)`.
- All database access goes through services, never directly in controllers.

## Auth

- JWT-based auth with http-only cookies.
- Use `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)` on protected endpoints.
- Access authenticated user via custom `@CurrentUser()` decorator.

## Testing

- Unit tests mock all dependencies via NestJS `Test.createTestingModule().overrideProvider().useValue()`.
- Integration tests (`.integration.test.ts`) use real database connections.
- Use `bun:test` (`describe`, `test`, `expect`).

## ESM

- The server runs as ESM. Use `.js` extensions in all relative imports.
- Use `reflect-metadata` for decorator support.
- TypeScript config enables `emitDecoratorMetadata` and `experimentalDecorators`.
